            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Jarvis 0.16.0</h2>
<p><b>Microsoft Teams joins your context.</b> Connect Teams in Settings and your
1:1 and group chats answer questions the same way Slack does — read live, never
stored. And when a source stops working, Jarvis now says so instead of quietly
returning less.</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Microsoft Teams (new).</b> Settings → Microsoft Teams, sign in, pick the
      chats Jarvis may read. Nothing from Teams is written to your Mac — every
      answer is fetched live and forgotten.</li>
  <li>Chats only, not channels: reading Teams channels always requires your
      admin's approval, so Jarvis does not ask for it.</li>
  <li><b>A source that stops working now says so.</b> A connection that expires
      or starts failing shows up on your day instead of silently going quiet.</li>
  <li>No changes to what leaves your Mac beyond the Teams chats you pick.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
